                "v": "<strong>Compensation: 4/5.</strong> Paying above median removes pay as a credible complaint — exit interviews confirm this directly (‘pay is fine’).<br><br><strong>Benefits: Unscored — no data given.</strong> This is itself a finding: if benefits were a problem, exit interviews would likely mention it. Absence of a signal isn't proof of strength, just lower priority for this diagnosis.<br><br><strong>Wellbeing: 2/5.</strong> ‘Unsustainable workload during close periods’ is a wellbeing red flag hiding inside what looks like an operations issue.<br><br><strong>Recognition: 2/5.</strong> A direct, frequent complaint about managers not acknowledging good work — this is acute, not background noise.<br><br><strong>Career Development: 1/5.</strong> The single most-cited theme. This is the dominant driver of the 28% turnover figure."
