                "v": "Age-based benefit de-prioritisation is a common error. Even a 31-year-old employee choosing between two otherwise comparable offers will notice a 3% total compensation difference once they understand it. The relevant question is not whether 31-year-olds actively think about retirement — most don't — but whether the benefit is visible at hiring and communicated clearly enough to affect the comparison. A Total Reward Statement that shows pension contribution as part of Total Compensation (as practised in the Course 1 capstone) makes the benefit real at offer stage, regardless of the employee's current retirement consciousness."
