                "v": "Post-IPO CEO pay structure:\n\n<strong>Base salary:</strong> Target at the median of a defined peer group (FTSE 250 professional services, 15 companies) to be established before IPO with remuneration committee sign-off. Reviewed annually using the same peer group.\n\n<strong>Annual bonus (STI):</strong> 100% of salary at target, 150% at maximum. 60% financial metrics (revenue growth, operating margin), 40% strategic objectives including a non-financial component. Deferred cash: 40% of any bonus deferred for 2 years in shares, vesting subject to continued employment.\n\n<strong>Long-term incentive (LTI):</strong> PSU plan. 150% of salary at target. 50% relative TSR vs peer group, 25% EPS growth, 25% non-financial (ESG/employee engagement). 3-year performance period + 2-year holding. Subject to a 15% maximum of issued share capital dilution limit (combined with all employee share schemes).\n\n<strong>Pension:</strong> 8% employer contribution, equal rate to average employee contribution rate (demonstrates pay ratio awareness from day one).\n\n<strong>Benefits:</strong> Healthcare, life insurance (3x salary), income protection. No special executive perquisites in the first year — these attract negative proxy advisor attention for new listcos."
