                "label": "See the reasoning",
                "v": "Let established quota = E and developing quota = D, where E = 1.6D.\n18E + 14D = £42M\n18(1.6D) + 14D = £42M\n28.8D + 14D = £42M\n42.8D = £42M\nD = £981,308 (approximately £980,000 per developing territory rep)\nE = 1.6 × £980,000 = £1,568,000 (approximately £1.57M per established territory rep)\n\nVerification: 18 × £1.57M + 14 × £980,000 = £28.26M + £13.72M = £41.98M ≈ £42M ✓\n\nThe approximately 60% premium for established territories reflects the lower development burden and richer account base — but should be tested against actual territory-specific data (account size, historical win rates) to confirm the 60% differential is appropriate rather than assumed."
