                "v": "<strong>Inside Sales (30 reps, mid-market $15-80K ACV):</strong> 55:45 pay mix. Active deal-making, shorter cycles, high individual attribution. TTC benchmark: survey mid-market SaaS inside sales in Nigeria market primarily. Target variable = 45% of base.\n\n<strong>Account Executives (30 reps, enterprise $100-500K ACV):</strong> 50:50 pay mix. Enterprise cycles are longer and more complex — but the deal sizes and individual revenue attribution justify high variable weighting. TTC benchmark: enterprise SaaS/fintech AEs across Nigeria, Kenya, UK depending on location. Target variable = 50% of base.\n\n<strong>Customer Success Managers (20 reps, renewal/expansion):</strong> 70:30 pay mix. Primary activity is relationship management and expansion — lower variable weighting reflects the lower attribution volatility. TTC benchmark: SaaS CSM market in each geography. Target variable = 30% of base.\n\n<strong>Sales Managers (6 managers):</strong> 65:35 pay mix. Management effectiveness component (25% of variable) + team revenue performance component (75% of variable). TTC benchmark: comparable SaaS sales management roles in each geography."
